version: v1.25.0
# Snyk policy file. Ignores below are reviewed decisions, not silenced defects.
ignore:
  'java/DisablesCSRFProtection':
    - 'src/main/java/io/spring/api/security/WebSecurityConfig.java':
        reason: >-
          The API is stateless: authentication is only ever established from a
          JWT in the Authorization request header (JwtTokenFilter), the session
          creation policy is STATELESS so no session cookie is issued, and CORS
          is configured with allowCredentials=false. No endpoint authenticates
          via a cookie or session, so a browser cannot be tricked into
          attaching ambient credentials and CSRF tokens add no protection.
        expires: 2027-08-10T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-10T00:00:00.000Z
  'java/SpringCSRF':
    - 'src/main/java/io/spring/api/ArticleApi.java':
        reason: >-
          Same root cause as java/DisablesCSRFProtection: stateless JWT
          (Authorization header) authentication with no cookie or session
          based auth anywhere in the application.
        expires: 2027-08-10T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-08-10T00:00:00.000Z
    - 'src/main/java/io/spring/api/ArticlesApi.java':
        reason: >-
          Same root cause as java/DisablesCSRFProtection: stateless JWT
